+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of `add`,
+`remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations) and returns the resulting document as a new
+value; neither the document nor the patch is mutated. It throws an `Error` if the patch is invalid
+(not an array, an operation that is not an object, an unknown `op`, a missing or non-string `path` or
+`from`, a missing `value` for `add`/`replace`/`test`) or if an operation fails (unresolved path, bad
+array index, failed `test`, removing the root, moving a value into its own child). The patch is
+atomic: on error nothing is returned. Tests: `npm test`.
